    "patchSets": [
        {
            "number": 1,
            "revision": "9cf9ebda582450dcf309eeda4366cc9289f11307",
            "parents": [
                "a93f3ea1a80a4d02983572f0ceb8b4692e2bd057"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/82/89182/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Eric Liu",
                "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                "username": "liuer-sys"
            },
            "createdOn": 1776056013,
            "author": {
                "name": "Eric Liu",
                "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                "username": "liuer-sys"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Every single one of those properties is already defined in `yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dimm.interface.yaml`, is it possible to drop the properties there to avoid the duplication?\n\ne.g. a reactor who previously exposed\n`xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.Dimm` could be changed to then\n\nexpose both\n`xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.Dimm` and\n`xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.Dram`\n\nwhere the updated `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.Dimm` would only hold properties not already provided by `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.Dram`.\n\nWhat do you think of this idea."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks! The current Item.Dram properties are a subset of Item.Dimm. The reason for creating a separate interface comes from the discussion on change 87221 (https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/87221/comment/f2d528d4_a14a51b0, where Ed Tanous pointed out:\n\n> \"DIMM isn't appropriate here. DIMM is a connector that fits into a slot. We'd need to come up with a dram inventory item.\"\n\nDeepak Kodihalli responded (https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/87221/comment/cb786d82_50fa6199/) suggesting that Item.Dimm is already used as Item.Memory in practice, and proposed renaming Item.Dimm to Item.Memory instead of creating a new interface.\n\n\n\nGiven that all 5 properties and 2 enums in Item.Dram are already defined in Item.Dimm, I agree the duplication should be resolved. I see two possible directions:\n\n1. Drop Item.Dram and rename Item.Dimm to Item.Memory (as Deepak suggested)\n2. Keep Item.Dram with the common properties and update Item.Dimm to remove the overlap\n\nHowever, both options would require updating existing Item.Dimm consumers (e.g. phosphor-host-ipmid, smbios-mdr, bmcweb). What is the recommended approach for handling this kind of PDI refactoring without breaking existing consumers? Thanks!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> What is the recommended approach for handling this kind of PDI refactoring without breaking existing consumers? Thanks!\n\nYou can create a gerrit topic to let maintainers know of related patches. The topic should also take effect in topic based CI for any repos based on generated headers."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "@liuer@nvidia.com Please take a look at @deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com's feedback in the dbus-sensors commit.  I agree with that sentiment."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @alexander.hansen@9elements.com , thanks for feedback.\nHi @patrick@stwcx.xyz, thanks for the feedback. Should we continue using Item.Dimm as-is for GPU embedded memory (HBM), or should we rename Item.Dimm to Item.Memory(or Item.Dram) as Deepak suggested in https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/87221/comment/cb786d82_50fa6199/? Thanks!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "If a rename is needed, I will follow Deepak's suggestion and submit a patch again to rename Item.Dimm to Item.Memory."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "A rename from Item.Dimm to Item.Memory doesn't look like an insignificant refactor.  Are you planning on making the change to all the corresponding repositories?\n\nIf we really are hung up on the name I'm ok with deprecating Dimm and transitioning to Memory while someone goes and fixes up all the existing uses.  You'd need to make bmcweb support both for a time.\n\nI don't think this rename is necessary but I'm also fine if we chose to go that route."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @patrick@stwcx.xyz\nThanks for your reply.\nI agree that renaming would have a significant impact \u2014 it touches all repos using this interface, involves multiple owners, and requires their help to update and verify.\n\nFor context, the original Item.Dram proposal was based on Ed Tanous's discussion in https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/87221/comment/f2d528d4_a14a51b0/ about the conceptual difference between DIMM and DRAM.\n\nHowever, I noticed that Item.Dimm already includes HBM/HBM2/HBM3 in its DeviceType enum (https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dimm.interface.yaml#L214-L222). Would it be appropriate to use Item.Dimm directly for GPU embedded memory (HBM)? Because rename could potentially have a very large impact.Thanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "I've summarized four possible options from the\ndiscussion so far:\n\nOption 1: Use Item.Dimm as-is for GPU HBM\n- No PDI change needed\n- Item.Dimm already has HBM/HBM2/HBM3 in DeviceType\n  enum\n- Simplest approach, no impact on existing consumers\n\nOption 2: Create Item.Memory, deprecate Item.Dimm(Thanks Harshit suggestion)\n- Copy Item.Dimm to Item.Memory\n- Mark Item.Dimm as deprecated\n- bmcweb supports both during the transition period\n- Other consumers can migrate at their own pace\n\nOption 3: Rename Item.Dimm to Item.Memory\n- Cleanest long-term\n- Requires updating all consumers at once\n  (phosphor-host-ipmid, smbios-mdr, bmcweb, etc.)\n- Can use a Gerrit topic to coordinate the change\n- Risk: involves multiple repos and owners, modifying\n  code maintained by others may introduce unexpected\n  issues\n\nOption 4: Keep Item.Dram with common properties,\n  update Item.Dimm to remove the overlap\n  (Thanks Alexander's suggestion)\n- Existing Item.Dimm consumers would expose both\n  Item.Dimm and Item.Dram\n- Item.Dimm only holds properties not in Item.Dram\n- Risk: requires updating all existing Item.Dimm\n  consumers to expose both interfaces, involves\n  multiple repos and owners, modifying code maintained\n  by others may introduce unexpected issues"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "In my personal opinion, option 2 is the best solution, as it doesn't affect the existing code and aligns with the ideas behind the other options."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Based on everyone's feedback, I went with Option 2 \u2014 creating Item.Memory and deprecating Item.Dimm. This approach combines the suggestions from the discussion. Please help review the updated patch.Thanks a lot.\n\nOption 2: Create Item.Memory, deprecate Item.Dimm\n- Copy Item.Dimm to Item.Memory\n- Mark Item.Dimm as deprecated\n- bmcweb supports both during the transition period\n- Other consumers can migrate at their own pace"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 27,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Both of the enums are also defined in Item.Dimm. Can we de-duplicate them."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dram.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 27,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks Harshit, I reply at below comment."
                }
            ],
