            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dimm.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 282,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "The current implementation in redfish-core/lib/memory.hpp expects a 1:1 mapping of these enums to Redfish enums, it appears, but the latest Redfish schema does not have \"Embedded\" as a type.  What do we plan to do?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dimm.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 282,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for the feedback.\n\nAfter further investigation: HBM and on-package LPDDR are both memory dies co-packaged with the host compute die in the same package. This matches the DMTF Memory schema [1] definition of BaseModuleType \"Die\": \"A die within a package\".\n\nPS7 removes the proposed \"Embedded\" enum value and uses the existing \"Die\" value instead. Please review the updated patch set, and let me know if there are any further concerns.\n\nMany thanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Dimm.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 282,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @patrick@stwcx.xyz\n\nWhenever you have a moment, would you mind taking another look at this? If you feel the current version is ready, I\u2019d be very grateful if you could help merge it. Many thanks for your time."
                }
            ],
